  "worked_solution": "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+2x$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({2}^{3}+{2}^{2})-((-2)^{3}+(-2)^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(12-(-4)) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
